_Last updated: 26 August 2026. Rewritten after the previous version stopped getting indexed by Google, most likely because it repeated the same aggregated global stats every other "SEO statistics" roundup uses. This version leads with real UK data, my own published research, and an honest explanation of why the industry's most-quoted numbers disagree with each other._

## Key SEO Statistics for 2026 (Quick Reference)

- Position 1 on Google earned **5.96% CTR** across 53 UK sites I manage, not the 25-30% still quoted in most decks (own data, 2026)
- The UK SEO and internet marketing consultancy industry generated **£24.6 billion** in revenue in 2025-26, growing at 6.6% a year (IBISWorld)
- Google holds **91-92%** of UK search share; Bing sits around 5.9-6.2% overall but climbs to nearly 13% on desktop (Statcounter, 2026)
- SEO leads close at **14.6%**, against 1.7% for outbound; the average organic lead costs $31 versus $181 for PPC (First Page Sage)
- **68.01%** of Google searches in the US ended without a click in the first four months of 2026, up from 60.45% in 2024 (SparkToro)
- Google AI Overviews now appear on anywhere from **20% to 48%** of tracked queries depending on whose study you read, and the range itself is the finding (Conductor, BrightEdge, First Page Sage, 2026)
- Only **48-49%** of mobile sites pass Core Web Vitals, up from 32% in 2021 (HTTP Archive)
- ChatGPT sent **91%** of AI referral traffic across 12 of my own sites over 90 days; Gemini sent 3 sessions total (own data, August 2026)

